      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "***SUPER LOCATION / OFF STREET PARKING / ATTIC CONVERSION / DOUBLE STORY EXTENSION***\r\n\r\nKELLY BRADSHAW are delighted to present No.30 Bargy Road, Eastwall, Dublin 3 to the market. \r\n\r\nThis extended three bedroom residence is located in the very popular and sought after location of East Wall in a quiet cul-de-sac off the main road. No.30 is very well presented and no stone has been left unturned in terms of renovations. \r\n\r\nBoasting generously proportioned accommodation throughout, this property has a well-designed floor plan and a great sense of space that has been extended to the front and rear and also benefits from a double story extension, along with an attic conversion. Bargy Road will appeal to those looking to move straight in and just unpack.\r\n\r\nOn entering, there is a paved gated driveway offering off street parking. There is an extended porch adding to the space in the hall. Off the welcoming hallway to the left is a tastefully decorated and very large living space. The living space is much larger than the norm and really is a fantastic hub for the whole family to gather. There are also two storage rooms in this space to cater for all your storage needs.\r\n\r\nThe kitchen to the rear has cream gloss presses and ample worktop space for all your cooking needs. The kitchen features patio doors that lead out to a low maintenance rear garden. Off the kitchen is a utility /lobby space that leads into a fully tiled bathroom.\r\n\r\nUpstairs the generous landing leads to 3 double bedrooms. The two bedrooms to the rear have been extended giving ample space. The master bedroom to the front benefits from a fully tiled en-suite.\r\n\r\nFinally completing the internal accommodation, the attic has been converted into a great light-filled space and is accessed via a Stira.\r\n\r\nEast Wall is a vibrant and active neighbourhood on the doorstep of the City Centre whilst still absorbing a quaint village feel and a most warming community spirit. The Sean O'Casey Centre is a great addition to the area offering a private gym, a community crèche and a wide range of events. \r\n\r\nThere is a choice of supermarkets nearby with Aldi and Lidl on your doorstep. East Point Business Park, Fairview and Clontarf seafront are also within a 10 minute walk and Dublin City Centre and Docklands are a leisurely 1km distance away. Public transport is in abundance with the area well catered for by Dublin Bus, LUAS, DART and Dublin Bikes.\r\n\r\nThis is a fantastic opportunity to acquire an extended 3 bedroom residence with the advantage of an attic conversion in the area where no work is required and the simple muted tones and layout should appeal to all that view. No.30 Bargy Road is a real winner in terms of location and as a spacious well-proportioned home."
      },
